2. Pass data between PEs: The PEs in the first row of the array pass their values to the PEs in the second row, and so on. This process continues until the values have been passed to the last row of the PEs.
3. Compute partial products: As the values are passed between PEs, each PE computes a partial product by multiplying its value with the value from the previous PE in the same column. The partial products are accumulated in a register or memory location associated with each PE.
4. Pass partial products: The PEs in each column pass their partial products to the PEs in the next column. This process continues until the partial products have been passed to the last column of the PEs.
5. Compute final products: As the partial products are passed between PEs, each PE computes the final product by adding its partial product with the partial products from the previous PEs in the same row. The final products are accumulated in a register or memory location associated with each PE.
6. Output the result: The final products are output from the PEs in the last row of the array, which represent the elements of the resulting matrix C.

